`log()` is a trigger function that prints the trigger name (and `NEW.id` for row-level triggers). Order the lines printed by the `INSERT`, first to last.

```sql
CREATE TRIGGER s_before BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER r_before BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER r_after  AFTER  INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();

INSERT INTO t VALUES (1), (2);
```

`log()` is a trigger function that prints the trigger name and `NEW.id`. All five are `BEFORE INSERT ... FOR EACH ROW` triggers on the same table, created in the order shown. Order the lines printed by the `INSERT`, first to last.

```sql
CREATE TRIGGER "trg_2"   BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER "audit"   BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER "trg_10"  BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER "Zeta"    BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();
CREATE TRIGGER "check_a" BEFORE INSERT ON t FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION log();

